# Build artifacts (DNA)
# Optional local Trinity CLI binary at repo root only (committed shim: scripts/tri)
/tri
zig-cache/
zig-out/
# gen/ hides the ~500 generated per-spec .zig files (real build output), but
# measure.py is hand-written tooling this project calls "the ONLY sanctioned
# instrument" for corpus correctness -- it had no git history at all until
# this exception, a single-machine single point of failure exactly like the
# one already found and fixed for the autonomous loop's own STATE.json. A
# bare `gen/` blanket-excludes the directory itself, which git will not
# traverse for `!` re-inclusion no matter how specific the negation --
# hence the `gen/*` / `gen/zig/*` wildcard form below instead.
gen/*
!gen/zig/
gen/zig/*
!gen/zig/measure.py
!gen/zig/test_measure.py
dist/
build/
target/

# Tooling
node_modules/
.turbo/
.npm/
.yarn/
bun.lockb
*.log
*.log.jsonl

# Secrets (local only; never commit)
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# OS
.DS_Store
*.swp
*.swo

# Temporary files
*.tmp
*.bak
*.orig
tmp/
.artifacts/

# Trinity State (should stay local/deterministic)
.trinity/claims/
.trinity/queues/
#.trinity/events/ # Keeping events might be okay if they are small, but they grow.

# Python cache
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Coq build byproducts (proofs/**); Rust build byproducts left outside target/
*.aux
*.glob
*.rlib
/t27c-built

# The three conflict markers that stood here were COMMITTED, at HEAD, unresolved
# ("<<<<<<< Updated upstream" / "=======" / ">>>>>>> Stashed changes"). git does
# not parse them: each was read as a literal pathspec, so the file kept working
# and nothing went red for however long it stood. Both sides are kept -- the
# upstream side is the three lines above, and the stashed side was character-for-
# character the "NotebookLM Gate" block that already appears below, so resolving
# it means deleting the duplicate, not choosing between them.

# Specific project paths (vendored upstream lives under external/)
external/opencode/dist/
external/opencode/node_modules/
external/opencode/packages/web/
bootstrap/target/
bootstrap/.trinity/
.trinity/experience/

# NotebookLM Gate — track essential files, ignore local session data
!.trinity/current_task/.notebook_id
!.trinity/current_task/notebook_meta.json
.trinity/current_task/session_log.jsonl
.trinity/gate_bypasses.log

# Vivado Docker build secrets (token + installer)
docker/wi_authentication_key
docker/FPGAs_AdaptiveSoCs_Unified_SDI_*.bin
docker/Xilinx_Unified_*.bin

# index_drift_scan.py's ratchet reference. Deliberately NOT tracked: it records
# which disk-vs-index disagreements were already present on ONE machine (here,
# 44 .trinity/seals case foldings that only exist because core.ignorecase=true,
# plus untracked Coq build outputs). None of that can occur on a fresh checkout,
# so committing it would hand every other clone one laptop's residue as the
# accepted state. The tool refuses to write one without --init, so an untracked
# baseline cannot silently re-mint itself (Prop. 211).
formal/index_drift_baseline.txt
